  "keyExceptions": {
    "CS-15": "Adopted practice interpretation: count successful loop-condition comparisons/iterations. These are floor(log2(n))+1. Counting the final false condition adds one, giving floor(log2(n))+2, which is absent from the printed options; supplied A fails at powers of two. Original examination scan p4 confirms the same printed defect.",
    "CS-24": "The ten even numbers are exchangeable; each has probability 1/10 of being first among them.",
    "CS-43": "A full n-ary tree has nI=I+L-1 edges. With I=10 and L=41, n=50/10=5.",
    "CS-48": "Every ordinary nonempty disjunctive clause is satisfied by a uniformly random assignment with probability at least 1/2. Expectation guarantees an assignment satisfying at least half the clauses. C contradicts this guarantee.",
    "CS-51": "Even composite n stops after its first divisor check, while prime n performs Theta(sqrt(n)) checks. Thus a uniform upper bound is O(sqrt(n)) and lower bound Omega(1). Treat the code as the intended C-like primality pseudocode despite its redundant printed declaration.",
    "CS-44": "Retain supplied A under the usual worst-case complexity interpretation; the literal number of recursive calls depends on n and m and can be zero.",
    "CS-54": "Retain supplied B for dependency-preserving code generation of the given basic block, without algebraic reassociation.",
    "CS-58": "Retain supplied D as the intended most specific statement: the protocol ensures mutual exclusion but can deadlock if both flags become true.",
    "CS-67": "C uses the historical exclusion of all-zero/all-one subnet identifiers. Modern 64-subnet/1022-host combination is absent from printed options.",
    "CS-69": "A uses the conventional Go-Back-N sliding-window interpretation; the variant is implicit in the question.",
    "CS-70": "B is the only option matching SMTP/application, TCP/transport and PPP/data-link. It classifies BGP by network-routing function, though BGP uses TCP.",
    "CS-78": "Original examination p20 has A->bAA, while the supplied reproduction p18 misprints S->bAA. Restore original grammar image; option C and two parse trees are unchanged.",
    "CS-79": "Evaluated only when CS-78 is correct; the accepted string aabbab has two parse trees (B). No deduction for wrong answer."
  },
